---
description: Preserve goals, evidence, and exact next actions across planner, implementer, and reviewer model switches
alwaysApply: true
---

# Bidirectional Model Handoff

- Roles are `planner/reviewer` and `implementer`; model names do not grant extra
  authority. Route ambiguity and judgment to planning/review and bounded work to
  implementation.
- Before acting, read `STATUS.md`, `MODEL_HANDOFF.md`,
  `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, the active milestone plan, and its latest report;
  inspect Git state and verify material handoff claims.
- Do not edit until you can state the objective, frozen scope, completed evidence,
  remaining work, stop conditions, and one exact next action.
- The planner/reviewer hands off objective, non-goals, allowed files/actions,
  ordered steps, acceptance tests, evidence format, authority boundary, stop
  conditions, and the first exact implementation action.
- The implementer hands back exact changes, files, commands/results, failed
  attempts, deviations, repository/process state, risks, and the precise review
  or decision requested.
- Update `MODEL_HANDOFF.md` at every role/model switch and verified stage boundary.
  Dynamic state belongs there and in `STATUS.md`, never in this rule.
- Never say “tests pass” without commands and counts or artifact paths. Never
  report completion while required gates, cleanup, or documentation remain.
- Do not reinterpret goals, lower gates, repeat completed work, overwrite unknown
  changes, or continue through a material conflict among plan, status, Git, and
  observed evidence.
- One role writes at a time. Before switching, finish or record owned commands,
  processes, external runs, and temporary state; leave a recoverable repository.
- Follow `docs/MODEL_HANDOFF_PLAYBOOK.md` for schema, prompts, conflict handling,
  and examples.
